Z||000000||Gokart||05-29-2000||02:53 PM||||OK! I know most of you are tired of my EGR woes but I'm going to clear this code 32 before my vacation is over! I got the right gasket with the steel insert and was told it goes at the plenum end of the tube. Today gtsonly told me he noticed this special gasket was at the VALVE end of his tube! This makes more sense because the material can withstand more heat which is at that end of the tube and maybe makes this steel insert functional? The instructions I printed from someone that bought a tube from the Fiero Store state: "Gasket with steel insert having small center hole MUST be installed at the inlet plenum end of the EGR valve adapter pipe assembly, with the side identified as tube side towards pipe assembly"! WHICH END  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> PLS HELP!<p>[This message has been edited by Gokart (edited 05-29-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Raydar||05-29-2000||11:19 PM||||The small hole goes on the plenum end. Not the exhaust system end. That's how my old one came off, and how I put the new one back.<BR>Everything that I've ever seen specified the same thing. ||||reg||1
